{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/95rqj2","slideIndex":0,"text":"Suggested narration (45–60 seconds):\nThe core drill system is already implemented. The React app talks to a Node and Express backend, which manages consent, drill attempts and scoring. Vapi coordinates voice calls: Claude generates the conversation, Deepgram transcribes speech and Azure Speech provides the Singapore-English voice. SMS uses Twilio; email uses Google Apps Script and MailApp. Supabase PostgreSQL stores progress and family data, and Realtime signals the apps to refresh. The repository configures Vercel for the frontend and serverless API.\n\nScope and accuracy: These are verified repository integrations, not a live production configuration audit. Claude defaults to claude-3-5-haiku-20241022; model and voice settings are overridable. Azure en-SG-WayneNeural is the default; ElevenLabs is an alternative. Twilio Verify is implemented, but the 2 October roadmap records a production demo verification bypass; resolve that before claiming verified ownership in real use. Supabase Auth is not used. SMS/email use curated templates. OpenAI GPT-5 mini exists in separate bulletin-extraction scripts, not the main drill call path. The automated Claude intelligence pipeline has all web sources disabled. Python folders are standalone earlier prototypes.\n\nSources inspected, 2 October 2026:\n/Users/ngwenjing/huawei-2026/package.json\n/Users/ngwenjing/huawei-2026/server/vapi.js\n/Users/ngwenjing/huawei-2026/server/sms.js\n/Users/ngwenjing/huawei-2026/server/verify.js\n/Users/ngwenjing/huawei-2026/server/email.js\n/Users/ngwenjing/huawei-2026/server/apps-script/Code.gs\n/Users/ngwenjing/huawei-2026/server/db.js\n/Users/ngwenjing/huawei-2026/server/doorbell.js\n/Users/ngwenjing/huawei-2026/src/app/house.ts\n/Users/ngwenjing/huawei-2026/vercel.json\n/Users/ngwenjing/huawei-2026/DEPLOY.md"}
